{
  "name": "wall_idle",
  "note": "(anim-rework S5 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced) Back to the wall, standing, holstered: square to the wall in the CT semi-crouch (knees 34 deg, the hips about 4 cm down), feet hip width, the pelvis and chest upright and tipped back 2 deg so the shoulder blades and the back of the head sit a small gap off the wall (the gap itself is the game's root push), the head turned about 30 deg to the open side (written for the open side on the RIGHT; the left is this clip mirrored), arms hanging close along the sides. Alive: two slow breaths, a small look along the open side (26-38 deg). Not mirrored. Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest. Arms: flex (+ forward, in the chest frame: the world angle is flex minus the chest pitch), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward; wrist (anim-rig, RIG.md) yaw / pitch / roll in the forearm frame, right hand as written, the left mirrored. Holstered arms; with a weapon drawn the arms stay procedural. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in toward the midline), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
